From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:38:36 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: cookie banners hidden without slowing frames down,
 and the page scrolls again

- The cookie list's rules for every site (~15,000 selectors, ~650 KB) are
  parsed once per renderer and shared by all its documents (one user style
  sheet, blink::WebDocument::InsertSharedStyleSheet), instead of a <style>
  element parsed again in every frame. Sent once per list as shared memory.
  A site's own rules (and a site with exceptions to the rules for every
  site) go in as a small sheet of the document's.
- Frames of other sites inside a page (ads, players, the popups' own
  frames) get only that site's own rules.
- Generic :has() rules are left out (on one site they stay).
- The rules go in before the document's first element, from the browser
  at ReadyToCommitNavigation (and again at DOMContentLoaded, kept if the
  same), as user style sheets the page's own !important can't undo.
- The scroll a consent popup locked comes back when its box is hidden:
  OneTrust, Didomi, Sourcepoint, Quantcast, Cookiebot, Usercentrics,
  TrustArc and others. Only while the popup's box is there and hidden, the
  page is locked by the popup's class, an inline style or a generic lock
  class, and no dialog of the site's own is open. A site's own modal still
  locks the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
